From: Canary233 <2096276316@qq.com>
Subject: netfilter: nf_conntrack: tolerate notifiers without exp_event

The QCA NSS ECM driver registers a struct nf_ct_event_notifier that only
implements .ct_event.  nf_ct_expect_event_report() calls ->exp_event()
unconditionally, so any conntrack expectation event (e.g. created by the
FTP helper for a forwarded connection) jumps to NULL and crashes the
kernel:

  pc : 0x0
  lr : nf_ct_expect_event_report+0x7c/0x9c [nf_conntrack]
  Call trace:
   nf_ct_expect_related_report
   nf_confirm
   ip_forward
   wg_packet_rx_poll

Skip the callback when the registered notifier does not provide it.

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_ecache.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_ecache.c
@@ -263,7 +263,8 @@ void nf_ct_expect_event_report(enum ip_c
 			.portid	= portid,
 			.report = report
 		};
-		notify->exp_event(1 << event, &item);
+		if (notify->exp_event)
+			notify->exp_event(1 << event, &item);
 	}
 out_unlock:
 	rcu_read_unlock();
